diff --git a/extensions/EGL_VENTURE_vulkan_creation_callbacks.txt b/extensions/EGL_VENTURE_vulkan_creation_callbacks.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..750eb15
--- /dev/null
+++ b/extensions/EGL_VENTURE_vulkan_creation_callbacks.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+EGL_VENTURE_vulkan_creation_callbacks (Venture private, version 1)
+
+This patch implements the creation-hook protocol proposed in Venture's
+2026-10-08 r3b-angle-vulkan report, "Concrete common initialization and frame
+protocol". It is not a Khronos-registered extension. The private token values
+0x51500001 and 0x51500002 must be kept out of guest-facing extension registries.
+
+Include EGL/eglext_angle_venture.h. Pass an EGLAttrib-sized pointer to an
+EGLVulkanCreationCallbacksVENTURE as the
+EGL_PLATFORM_ANGLE_VULKAN_CREATION_CALLBACKS_VENTURE display attribute to the
+EGL 1.5 eglGetPlatformDisplay function. Do not use the EGLint-sized attribute
+list of eglGetPlatformDisplayEXT: it truncates pointers on 64-bit hosts.
+Explicit EGL_PLATFORM_ANGLE_ANGLE and EGL_PLATFORM_ANGLE_TYPE_VULKAN_ANGLE are
+required. Zero selects unmodified stock behavior.
+
+The client extension string advertises availability. The table's version must
+be 1, size must be at least sizeof(the version 1 table), and all four functions
+must be non-null. Invalid tables make eglInitialize fail with EGL_BAD_ATTRIBUTE.
+The pointer must refer to readable host memory. It is part of display identity:
+different table pointers produce distinct displays. Keep the table address,
+contents, callback code and userData valid and unchanged throughout the display's
+lifetime, including reinitialization after eglTerminate. ANGLE copies the table
+at initialization; it never invokes guest machine code.
+
+Callbacks are synchronous on the initializing thread. Do not throw exceptions
+across this C ABI or reenter EGL/GLES. The create-info structures, pNext chains,
+extension name arrays and allocator are borrowed only for the call. The loader
+argument is the real Vulkan resolver used by ANGLE, not ANGLE's device-query
+resolver (whose create functions are wrappers). In an XR_KHR_vulkan_enable2
+integration pass this resolver to xrCreateVulkanInstanceKHR and
+xrCreateVulkanDeviceKHR, and check both XrResult and VkResult. The physical-device
+callback can call xrGetVulkanGraphicsDevice2KHR. Its returned handle must be one
+of the supplied instance's enumerated devices; otherwise initialization fails,
+without falling back to another GPU.
+
+Preserve all ANGLE-requested features, extensions, queue create infos, and Vulkan
+API requirements. An XR runtime may add requirements. The integration must obey
+the XR API-version bounds; return VK_ERROR_INCOMPATIBLE_DRIVER for an empty
+intersection. If additions need to be recorded, wrap the supplied resolver when
+passing it to OpenXR, as described by the enable2 specification. The existing
+EGL_VULKAN_*_EXTENSIONS_ANGLE / FEATURES_ANGLE queries describe ANGLE's requests,
+not additions made inside the callbacks. The caller owns that final record.
+
+On failure return a Vulkan error with a null output handle; ANGLE translates it
+through its existing error path. Successful instance/device creation immediately
+transfers ownership to ANGLE, including cleanup if a later initialization step
+fails. ANGLE destroys them with its original allocator. They must be created
+through the supplied loader and must not be destroyed by the caller.
+
+Callback mode creates one unprotected graphics queue. Context-priority and
+protected-content extensions are not advertised in this mode. deviceReady
+reports the actual VkQueue, queue family and queue index after queue retrieval.
+These are borrowed handles, usable only after eglInitialize succeeds and before
+eglTerminate. Destroy XR sessions/swapchains and other borrowers before terminating
+ANGLE. A later initialization failure invalidates the deviceReady handles.
+
+eglQueryDeviceAttribEXT accepts EGL_VULKAN_QUEUE_INDEX_VENTURE and returns the
+index of the queue already exposed by EGL_VULKAN_QUEUE_ANGLE (Medium priority).
+The existing, misspelled EGL_VULKAN_QUEUE_FAMILIY_INDEX_ANGLE returns its family.
+This query also works for stock displays; stock queue-selection policy is unchanged.
+
+Share the queue using eglLockVulkanQueueANGLE / eglUnlockVulkanQueueANGLE around
+external queue operations; never hold that lock while calling GLES entrypoints
+that submit. This is CPU external synchronization, not GPU completion. This
+extension does not change image import, image layout, submission or XR swapchain
+lifetime rules and is not a general external-device adoption API.
